::ENG3_U02_L08_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG3.W.01] Review passage: The abandoned station stood between the old farms and the new factories. In a poem written during the town's industrial shift, one speaker calls the station "a locked mouth full of departures." A later essay from the same period argues that the station brought wages but carried away memory. Which narrative perspective would best extend the same conflict? {
=A. A former farm worker who needs factory wages but misses the old community.#Correct. This perspective holds both economic need and memory, matching the conflict. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~B. A traveler who has no connection to farms, factories, wages, or memory.#This would not extend the central conflict well. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
